'''''Campanula lasiocarpa''''', also known as the '''mountain harebell''' or '''Alaska harebell''',<ref>{{cite web|title=Campanula lasiocarpa|url=https://www.cdhs.us/Flower%20Project/Family%20Index/Campanulaceae%20Index/Campanula%20lasiocarpa/C.%20lasiocarpa%20Frameset.htm|publisher=Circle District Historical Society|accessdate=July 11, 2013}}</ref> is a species of flowering plant. It is native to eastern Russia, Japan, the northwestern portion of North America including the US states of [[Alaska]] and [[Washington (state)|Washington]], as well as the Canadian provinces of [[Alberta]], [[British Columbia]], the [[Northwest Territories]], and the [[Yukon]].<ref>{{cite web|title=PLANTS Profile for Campanula lasiocarpa (mountain harebell)|url=https://plants.usda.gov/java/profile?symbol=cala7|publisher=USDA|access-date=July 11, 2013}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Campanula lasiocarpa Cham. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:140561-1 |access-date=2025-08-31 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref>

